agent_variants/deepseek_harness/node_modules

# `data/` is mostly baseline worlds the image does not need, but the frozen structured-v1
# freeze manifest is a build input: `agent_image/Dockerfile` copies it, and the documented
# build command points at it as `data/structured-v1/freeze-manifest.json`.
#
# A single `!data/structured-v1/freeze-manifest.json` would not work.  Docker does not
# re-include a path inside an excluded directory, so excluding `data` outright makes that file
# invisible and the documented command fails with "file not found in build context".  The
# exclusion therefore has to be opened one level at a time, which is what the next four lines
# do.  It used to be a plain `data`, and the workaround was a second copy of the manifest under
# `agent_image/` -- two files that had to be kept identical by hand, which is the drift this
# avoids.
data/*
!data/structured-v1
data/structured-v1/*
!data/structured-v1/freeze-manifest.json
